              {
                "annotations": [],
                "text": "Answering the task with the following logic:\n1. Find the horizontal line of 2s.\n2. The grid has two other colored rows: the top row (row 0) and the bottom row (row H-1).\n3. Find the horizontal span/interval [min_col, max_col] of the non-zero colored pixels in the top row, and similarly for the bottom row.\n4. The column range for 4 is the intersection of these two intervals: `[max(min_col_top, min_col_bottom), min(max_col_top, max_col_bottom)]`.\n5. Count the number of non-zero colored pixels in the top row vs the bottom row.\n   - If top row has more pixels, place 4s in all rows between row 0 and the line of 2s.\n   - If bottom row has more pixels, place 4s in all rows between the line of 2s and the bottom row.\n   (In both cases, 4s are placed in the intersecting column range).",
